# Caddy sits behind ts-portainer's TCPForward+TerminateTLS serve config.
# Tailscale terminates TLS on the tailnet-facing side (443) using its own
# automatic cert for portainer.${TS_TAILNET_DOMAIN}, then forwards the
# decrypted plaintext HTTP as a raw TCP stream to Caddy on 8444 — this port
# is never published to the host, it's only reachable via the shared
# network namespace (network_mode: service:ts-portainer) from ts-portainer's
# loopback.
#
# Caddy exists here purely to do the actual HTTP-level reverse proxying,
# since tailscaled's own built-in Web/Proxy serve mode is documented as
# 5-10x slower under concurrent load (tailscale/tailscale#18307) — confirmed
# 2026-08-03 as an accept-then-hang on any response above a trivial size
# (small JSON responses worked, the full HTML UI did not), on both the
# tailnet HTTPS URL and the "direct" published port:9000 path — both were
# being relayed through tailscaled's own userspace proxy since no real
# tailscale0 kernel interface exists in this container. Caddy doesn't need
# its own TLS cert or config beyond this — the tailnet-facing TLS is
# entirely Tailscale's job.
:8444 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9000
}
